STANDING ORDER - CONCEALMENT AND VISIBILITY

The red cloud is a signal. It is shown only when the Leader wills the organisation
to be seen.

- On covert movement through villages or contested territory, wear the issued
  conical hat and paper veil. Conceal the cloak. Draw no attention to the pattern.
- Do not announce membership. Do not speak the organisation's name where it may be
  overheard. A rumour of the Dawn travels faster than any of us.
- When an operation calls for fear - when the Leader wants a village to know who took
  their beast - the cloaks come out, and not before.
- Hosts and Kage should learn we exist only when it is too late to matter.

Visibility is a weapon. Spend it on the Leader's word, never your own vanity.
